## Managed Identity + RBAC

Assigned a System-assigned Managed Identity to the VM.

The VM's identity was given:

```text
Storage Blob Data Contributor
```

at the Storage Account scope.

Concept:

```text
Managed Identity
    ↓
Authentication
    ↓
Access Token
    ↓
RBAC
    ↓
Authorization
    ↓
Blob access
```

Important distinction:

```text
Authentication = Who are you?

Authorization = What are you allowed to do?
```
az role assignment create \
  --assignee-object-id "$PRINCIPAL_ID" \
  --assignee-principal-type ServicePrincipal \
  --role "Storage Blob Data Contributor" \
  --scope "$STORAGE_ID"

---

## Blob Access Tier

Initial Blob tier:

```text
Hot
```

Manually changed:

```text
Hot → Cool
```

Verified with the Blob response:

```text
x-ms-access-tier: Cool
```

Important:

> Changing one Blob's tier does not change the Storage Account's default tier.

---

## Lifecycle Management

Configured:

```text
Target:
web-logs/

Blob type:
Block Blob

Condition:
More than 30 days since modification

Action:
Hot → Cool
```

Purpose:

> Automatically move older logs to a lower-cost access tier.

Lifecycle Management is different from manually changing a Blob's tier.

